    "q-129936": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129936",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{{y}^{2}+1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[1,e]\\times [0,3].$",
      "worked_solution": "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{{y}^{2}+1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{x})({y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{3}({y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{e}\\cdot [\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+y]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\cdot (\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}+3) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
